    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Corbin Carroll**, whose score of 77.88 makes him our definitive start of the day. Facing Michael McGreevy (xERA 4.53) with an assumed #3 spot in the lineup, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a strong SP skill matchup and an elite dynamic platoon advantage that elevates his floor significantly. **Josh Naylor** (65.02) follows closely as a primary source of run production; his matchup against Chandler is ideal, as the combination of middle-order placement and favorable platoon dynamics offsets the neutral park factor. While **Gabriel Moreno** (61.48) and **Jose Caballero** (59.98) sit on the cusp of \"Strong\" territory, both offer high-value upside, with **Jose Caballero** notably utilizing a +13% platoon edge against Connelly Early to overcome a tough SP skill matchup.\n\nOur decision-making process for the remaining slots remains heavily influenced by our prioritization of speed and efficiency. We are closely monitoring the lineup postings for **Max Muncy** and **Zach McKinstry**, who both currently reside in the \"Marginal\" range due to lower lineup placement (#8). **Tyler Soderstrom** (57.66) remains a high-floor play, providing solid utility despite the challenging matchup against Landen Roupp. No players currently on the bench pose an immediate threat to the starting configuration, as our primary depth pieces\u2014including **Mickey Moniak**, **Brice Turang**, and **Austin Riley**\u2014are sidelined due to schedule gaps, while **Trevor Story** remains unavailable on the IL. We remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for almost all starters; should defensive shifts or last-minute rest impact the projected batting order, we may need to re-evaluate the efficiency of **Max Muncy** to ensure we aren't burning limited game caps on suboptimal slot production.",
